<Layout title="Maryland Guide" active="Maryland Guide"><div class="page-top"><h1>Maryland competition guide</h1><p>What Glenelg Country School members need to know for the 2026–2027 season. Your chapter is in Central District.</p></div><div class="guide-grid"><article class="prose"><h2>Your district dates</h2><ul class="date-list"><li><time datetime="2026-10-27">October 27</time><span>District registration deadline. Confirm registration with your adviser.</span></li><li><time datetime="2026-10-31">October 31</time><span>Pre-judged district materials due.</span></li><li><time datetime="2026-11-09">November 9–12</time><span>Objective testing window, 7 a.m.–5 p.m. Eastern. Tests are proctored at school.</span></li><li><time datetime="2026-11-21">November 21</time><span>Central District Leadership Conference at Howard High School, 10 a.m.–4 p.m. Follow your assigned event schedule.</span></li></ul><p class="small">Checked October 27, 2026 · <a href="https://www.mdfbla.org/dlc" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Maryland conference source ↗</a> · <a href="https://www.mdfbla.org/chapters" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Chapter district directory ↗</a></p><h2>Check your event’s district format</h2><p>Maryland districts are a qualifying stage. Some events use a different format at states or nationals. Every event guide here opens with district preparation and lets you switch stages.</p><table><thead><tr><th>District format</th><th>What to prepare</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Objective test · 45 events</td><td>Study the published knowledge areas. Marketing, for example, uses a district test; its role play comes at states.</td></tr><tr><td>Pre-submitted work · 13 events</td><td>Prepare a 5–10-slide presentation exported to PDF. Coding & Programming is an example. Check the event’s pre-judge rubric.</td></tr><tr><td>Live presentation · 15 events</td><td>Prepare the required project, speech, or interview and practise its timing. Check for any additional pre-judged asset.</td></tr><tr><td>Starts at states · 3 events</td><td>Computer Applications, Community Service Project, and Local Chapter Annual Business Report have no district competition.</td></tr></tbody></table><p class="small"><a href="https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1yDlT1ij5CEVK3AzXCFHuotvjCEsBwXsn/edit" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Maryland’s full event comparison ↗</a></p><h2>How to study</h2><ol><li><strong>Choose your event and stage.</strong> Read the format, eligible grades, team size, and any special conditions.</li><li><strong>Learn one topic.</strong> Read a lesson, work through the example, and explain the key terms aloud.</li><li><strong>Check recall.</strong> Answer the lesson check, then read the explanation. Use the flashcards to review key terms.</li><li><strong>Save what needs more work.</strong> Bookmark lessons you want to review and use the printable quick-review page as the conference approaches.</li></ol><h2>After districts</h2><p>The current Maryland state page lists registration closing December 18, 2026, and pre-judged materials due January 15, 2027. State objective testing is listed as onsite. Confirm qualification and the event you will enter with your adviser.</p><p><a href="https://www.mdfbla.org/slc" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">State conference details ↗</a></p><h2>When two sources disagree</h2><p>Use Maryland’s current guide for Maryland-specific administration and the national guide for national competition. A current-season file can still contain an old date. The Accounting page flags a coursework eligibility date conflict. Ask your adviser to confirm unresolved requirements.</p></article><aside class="event-sidebar"><h3>Official links</h3><a class="source-label" href="https://www.mdfbla.org/dlc" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">District conference information ↗</a><a class="source-label" href="https://www.mdfbla.org/competitive-events" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Maryland event guides ↗</a><a class="source-label" href="https://www.mdfbla.org/slc" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">State conference information ↗</a><a class="source-label" href="https://connect.fbla.org/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">FBLA CONNECT ↗</a><h3 style="margin-top:30px">Your competition work</h3><p>Use these lessons to learn the skills. Read your event’s original prompt and assistance rules before creating your submission.</p><p class="inline-alert">This website does not register competitors, submit files to Blue Panda, or replace your adviser’s instructions.</p></aside></div></Layout>

